title: Next month
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.advisor_action_timer <= 0) {
    Q.pinnedCardsDescription = 'Advisors - an action is available';
} else if (Q.advisor_action_timer == 1) {
    Q.pinnedCardsDescription = 'Advisors - next action available in 1 week';
} else {
    Q.pinnedCardsDescription = 'Advisors - next action available in ' + Q.advisor_action_timer + ' weeks';
}
if (Q.shuffle_leadership_timer <= 0) {
    Q.pinnedCardsDescription += '\n- a reshuffle is available.';
} else if (Q.shuffle_leadership_timer == 1) {
    Q.pinnedCardsDescription += '\n- next reshuffle in 1 week';
} else {
    Q.pinnedCardsDescription += '\n- next reshuffle in ' + Q.shuffle_leadership_timer + ' weeks.';
}
Q.last_time_updated = Q.time;
Q.last_week_updated = Q.week;
!}
new-page: true
###/// basic timed news element template: [? if year == year and month == month and week == week : text <div>Options Button</div> ?]
###/// Delete later: You can work with the farmers in Schleswig to lobby for price floors, or emergency aid for farmers, or do nothing. 
###///# The first option increases spd rural by 2, and shifts Agricultural parties left, as well as forming a SSBB (Sozialdemokratische Schleswig Bauern Bund) in Schleswig, which provides a passive buff & floor to rural support. Additionally if the DBP left > 3, the SSBB merges into the DBP in March, increasing thier vote share by a tiny percent during elections, and pushing them left, and should unlock a secret option for (one of) the DBP congress. However, this decreases worker support by 1 (Shifting to the DDP), and provides a passive buff to DDP worker support and floor if SPD worker vote is >55
###///# The sceond option increases rural support by 1, and increases the rural support gain from any non-base faction economic plan by 0.1, so this buff is only useful if you want to go something that isn't one of the abse factions or AgSoc (The first option would be better for agsoc)

= Week [+ week +], Month [+ month +]([+ month : month +]), Year [+ year +]

